3. Machine Learning Model Results (MNIST Clustering)
For the computer vision component of the project, an unsupervised machine learning approach was utilized. Note: As the project objective was to evaluate the efficacy of a specific unsupervised grouping technique, only a single model (K-Means) was developed; therefore, a multi-model comparative analysis is not applicable.
Model Setup and Validation
A K-Means clustering algorithm was applied to the MNIST handwritten digits dataset (1,797 image samples, 64 pixel features each). The model was initialized with n_clusters=10 to represent the digits 0 through 9. Because K-Means is unsupervised and assigns arbitrary cluster labels, a mapping function using the statistical mode was applied to align the predicted clusters with the true ground-truth labels for evaluation.
Prediction Accuracy Metric
The overall performance of the clustering algorithm was measured using a Macro-Averaged F1 Score. This metric was chosen to ensure a balanced evaluation of precision and recall evenly across all 10 digit classes.
Achieved Macro-Averaged F1 Score: 0.7895 (or 78.95%)
